            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for to envy, then the German for to not begrudge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: die Scham",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Scham — \"shame\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Vor Scham wurde sie ganz rot. She went bright red with shame."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "No plural. Vor Scham — with shame."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Scham is inherited from Old High German scama, from Proto-Germanic skamō \"shame\" (EtymDB); English shame is a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
