          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "verlegen — \"embarrassed, sheepish\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Der Junge lächelte verlegen und sagte nichts. The boy smiled sheepishly and said nothing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "There is also a verb verlegen — to misplace, or to move to another date: Ich habe meine Brille verlegt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The adjective verlegen is usually traced to Middle High German verlegen, the past participle of verligen \"to lie too long, to grow sluggish\", built on liegen \"to lie\"; EtymDB records only the verb verlegen \"to misplace\"."
            }
          ]
        },
